<h2>Where should the filters go on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">These are wireframes. They show placement only, not final styling. All three filter in the browser and show a live result count above the table.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Toolbar above the table</h3>
      <p>Event type (Select, all nine types) and a search box for device or location, always visible between the intro and the table.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:flex-end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:8px">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Event type<select class="mock-input"><option>All events</option><option>Sign-in failed</option></select></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Search device or location<input class="mock-input" type="search" placeholder="e.g. Madrid, iPhone"></label>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px"><em>Showing 14 of 52 events</em></p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Toolbar plus a "Failed sign-ins" shortcut</h3>
      <p>Same as A, with a one-click toggle for failed sign-ins, since that is what people (and Security) look for most. The active filter shows as a removable tag.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:flex-end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:8px">
            <button class="mock-button">Show failed sign-ins only</button>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Event type<select class="mock-input"><option>All events</option></select></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Search device or location<input class="mock-input" type="search" placeholder="e.g. Madrid, iPhone"></label>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Filtered by: <span class="mock-button" style="padding:2px 8px">Sign-in failed &times;</span> &nbsp;<em>Showing 6 of 52 events</em></p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>"Filter" button that opens a popover</h3>
      <p>Keeps the page header clean. The same fields live in a popover, and the active filters show as tags next to the button.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:8px">
            <button class="mock-button">Filter (1)</button>
            <span class="mock-button" style="padding:2px 8px">Sign-in failed &times;</span>
            <em>Showing 6 of 52 events</em>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:8px;margin:0 0 8px;max-width:260px">
            <div style="margin-bottom:6px">Event type<br><select class="mock-input"><option>Sign-in failed</option></select></div>
            <div>Search device or location<br><input class="mock-input" type="search"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
